{
  "requirement": "`habeas status` and the mdBook requirements index MUST generate their Definition/Evidence Markdown tables through the same renderer. That renderer MUST calculate column widths, align the columns, and display the same evidence-state labels in both outputs. Callers MAY select different definitions and supply different kind-labeled name cells so mdBook can link to detail pages.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "No gaps found. Both outputs build their Definition/Evidence tables through `render_evidence_table`, and the code and tests below carry out each clause.\n\n**Obligations**\n1. `habeas status` and the mdBook requirements index MUST generate their tables through the same renderer.\n   - `status_markdown_with_github` (src/commands.rs) pushes `(name cell, evidence.state().label())` rows and calls `render_evidence_table(&rows)`. It carries `{impl}` references to the subject, at the function and at the call site. `status_markdown_with_options` carries the same reference.\n   - `DetailPlan::populate` (src/index.rs) builds its rows the same way and calls `render_evidence_table(&rows)`. It is also marked with `{impl}`.\n2. The renderer MUST calculate column widths. `render_evidence_table` (src/markdown.rs, marked `{impl}`) takes the maximum cell length of each column, with minimums of \"Definition\" and \"Evidence\" for the headers.\n3. The renderer MUST align the columns. The header, separator and data rows are all padded to those widths with `{:<width$}`.\n4. The renderer MUST display the same evidence-state labels in both outputs. Both callers pass `evidence.state().label()`, which is `EvidenceState::label` in src/index.rs and has one definition. The renderer displays the labels it is given unchanged.\n5. Callers MAY select different definitions and supply different name cells. Status filters by glob, `--all` and verbose and uses plain backticked names. The index uses all detail pages and supplies linked names such as `[`name`](href) (kind)`. MAY imposes nothing to check.\n\n**Tests**\n- `index_shows_evidence_states_and_links_generated_chapters` (src/index.rs) carries `{test}` for the subject. It checks the index table's state labels (Valid, Determination false, Invalid, Missing) and that every row's pipe positions match the header's. It also checks the linked name cells.\n- The status side is exercised by `status_tables_align_each_column_to_its_widest_cell`, which checks pipe alignment, column width equal to the widest cell, and the `---` separator, in both default and `--all` modes. The tests in tests/commands.rs check the state labels and name cells in the status table. These are marked for `requirements.cli.status_table_alignment` and `requirements.cli.status`, not for this subject.\n- I did not count the missing `{test}` marking on the status-side tests as a gap. They cover the more specific alignment and status requirements, and the single shared renderer's width, alignment and label behavior is directly tested through the index test.\n\nI found no unspecified behavior in the renderer.",
  "references": "7c5c069787268914ddbc6961b51a8599de95ed7436f28a4dacec76f391365fc9",
